# Communication app status

Updated: 2026-11-14

## Implemented

- Private conversations and persistent messages using Django's configured user model.
- `open_conversation()`, `close_conversation()` and `mark_trip_completed()` integration services.
- Participant-only chat pages, one-second message polling, read receipts and sender-only soft deletion.
- Twenty-four-hour chat expiry and the `close_conversations` management command.
- Reviews limited to completed trips and their participants; one review per person per trip.
- Rating summaries hidden until three reviews, staff review moderation and CSV export.
- Whole-word moderation with basic accent, repetition and character-substitution normalization.
- Responsive communication pages and tests for permissions, messaging, reviews, moderation and exports.

## Integration limits

- The reservations and trips apps do not yet define models or call the communication services. Until they do, conversations must be created through `open_conversation()` and trips marked complete through `mark_trip_completed()`.
- Django Channels and Redis are not configured. Chat uses HTTP polling once per second instead of WebSockets.
- Configure `COMMUNICATION_BLOCKED_TERMS` in Django settings or the `CORIDE_BLOCKED_TERMS` environment variable. No moderation vocabulary is bundled, and an ML classifier is not implemented.
- Only CSV review export is available; PDF and Excel require additional dependencies.

## Checks

```powershell
uv run manage.py check
uv run manage.py test communication
uv run manage.py makemigrations --check --dry-run
```
